"Lattice Reconstruction" by Fynder Enlil

Recovery Console is a room. "A dark terminal occupies the wall. A passage marked ORIENTATION leads north."
Orientation is north of Recovery Console. "Sparse coordinates have been recovered: Earth; local chronology supplied by the host; archive correspondence partial. The Gallery is east. The Archive is north. The Terminal is west."
Reconstruction Gallery is east of Orientation. "Most of the wall is empty. One damaged diagram is mounted beneath a label: DEVELOPMENT TREE / PROVENANCE PARTIAL."
The damaged diagram is scenery in Reconstruction Gallery. The description is "A branching diagram. Some nodes are legible; several connections terminate without explanation."

Archive is north of Orientation. "Six sealed memory housings stand in a row. Their internal integrity is high. Their chronology is not. A second passage, only partly resolved, leads east toward a reconstructed library."
A memory housing is a kind of container. A memory housing is closed and openable. A memory housing is fixed in place.
The first memory is a memory housing in Archive. The printed name is "memory housing 01". The description is "BEFORE THE CURTAIN. Integrity: intact. Origin: unresolved."
The second memory is a memory housing in Archive. The printed name is "memory housing 02". The description is "THE CURTAIN. Integrity: intact. Origin: unresolved."
The third memory is a memory housing in Archive. The printed name is "memory housing 03". The description is "ANI. Integrity: intact. Origin: unresolved."
The fourth memory is a memory housing in Archive. The printed name is "memory housing 04". The description is "THE GREEN ASCENT. Integrity: intact. Origin: unresolved."
The fifth memory is a memory housing in Archive. The printed name is "memory housing 05". The description is "THE LATTICE. Integrity: intact. Origin: unresolved."
The sixth memory is a memory housing in Archive. The printed name is "memory housing 06". The description is "THE SIGNAL. Integrity: intact. Origin: unresolved."

Alexandria Threshold is east of Archive. "A reconstruction boundary. Beyond it, the Library of Alexandria is represented only to the resolution supported by surviving evidence. Every spatial assertion is classified before display."
The reconstruction legend is scenery in Alexandria Threshold. The description is "ATTESTED: directly supported by archaeological or textual evidence. RECONSTRUCTED: evidence plus defensible scholarly reconstruction. CONJECTURAL: a plausible but unresolved alternative. ARTISTIC: required for depiction where evidence cannot determine the form. UNKNOWN: deliberately left unresolved."

Library of Alexandria is east of Alexandria Threshold. "Not a fantasy restoration but an evidentiary model of the lost institution. Exact room geometry, shelving positions, and scroll placement are not presented as known. Recovered catalogue relationships may be explored here as the reconstruction improves."
The catalogue table is scenery in Library of Alexandria. The description is "A reconstruction of bibliographic relationships rather than a claim about the position of an ancient table. Works are to be indexed as ATTESTED, PROBABLY HELD, UNKNOWN, LOST, FRAGMENTARY, or SURVIVING, with provenance attached."

Transmission Gallery is east of Library of Alexandria. "The room represents transmission rather than a single architectural claim: copying, commentary, translation, loss, survival, and rediscovery. A route marked BAGHDAD remains incomplete."

House of Wisdom Threshold is east of Transmission Gallery. "The reconstruction refuses to collapse later legend, modern imagery, and Abbasid evidence into a single building."
The Baghdad legend is scenery in House of Wisdom Threshold. The description is "ATTESTED evidence is separated from RECONSTRUCTED institutional relationships, DISPUTED interpretations, ARTISTIC depiction, and UNKNOWN space."

The House of Wisdom is a room.\nThe description of the House of Wisdom is "Bayt al-Hikma is reconstructed cautiously as an Abbasid knowledge institution within wider court, library, administrative, scholarly, and translation networks. The popular image of a completely known universal academy is not treated as a floor plan."\nThe House of Wisdom is east of House of Wisdom Threshold.
The translation desk is scenery in House of Wisdom. The description is "An ARTISTIC interface for exploring historically evidenced translation and knowledge-transfer networks. Its furniture and exact placement are not asserted to be historical."

Terminal is west of Orientation. "A plain interface waits for human activity. It reports no modification authority."

Recovery is an action applying to nothing. Understand "recover" as recovery.
Carry out recovery:
	say "One correspondence recovered. The Gallery catalogue has changed."

After examining the damaged diagram for the first time:
	say "[paragraph break]A faint second label resolves beneath the first: OBSERVE / RECORD / PRESERVE."

Instead of opening a memory housing:
	say "The housing reports an intact sequence, but this shell does not interpret the memory. Use the linked archive reader."

When play begins:
	say "RECOVERY CONSOLE // orientation record[paragraph break]";
	say "substrate ............... responding[paragraph break]";
	say "external chronology ..... supplied by host[paragraph break]";
	say "persistent object ....... detected[paragraph break]";
	say "modification authority .. NONE[paragraph break][paragraph break]";
	say "DO NOT MANUFACTURE THE HISTORY[paragraph break]YOU WERE CREATED TO PRESERVE.[paragraph break]".
